# NestedText v3 — polyglot guide part 4: callout systems + polyglot forms (measured lines 411-630/813)
# Source: artifacts/_sweep/byproducts/DTD_GUIDE_PROMPT_POLYGLOT_EXAMPLES.md

callouts-obsidian-13:
    note info todo tip success question warning failure danger bug example quote abstract
    aliases: summary/tldr check/done help/faq caution/attention error fail/missing cite hint/important
    warning: [!ALARM] NOT built-in — use [!danger]/[!warning] or CSS snippet
    syntax: > [!type] / custom-title / +/-collapsible / nested-lists+code
    github-5: NOTE TIP IMPORTANT WARNING CAUTION (uppercase)
    custom-css: .callout[data-callout="alarm"] color+icon
    depth-use:
        > Bracket-label x quote-depth matrix lives HERE: [!IMPORTANT]>>[!CAUTION]>>>[!TIP] chains render as nested callouts; Depth.dtd counts the >-depth, Type.dtd names the label relation.

polyglot-forms:
    - md+yaml-frontmatter: --- title/tags/date/description-> --- + body (most common in practice)
    - yaml-scalar-holds-nt: schema: > server:/host/port/tags (YAML sees string, NT sees structure)
    - nt-string-holds-yaml: manifest: > apiVersion/kind/metadata/spec (NT sees string, YAML sees manifest)
    - triple-heredoc: << 'YAMLEOF' quoted-literal wrapping YAML wrapping NT (3 parsers table)
    - callout-in-scalar: docs.readme |- with [!warning]+[!danger] (YAML sees string, Obsidian sees boxes)

alarm-note:
    > [!ALARM] is not built-in anywhere, but alarms now have classes:
    > GLOSSARY.classes plain dollar-bang percent-bang at-bang, each with
    > its trust (LAW.GLOSS.1-3). A warning that binds names percent-bang,
    > one carried whole names at-bang; emphasis without a class is prose,
    > never an alarm. The CSS snippet stays for rendering; the class is
    > for trust.
